From abe56cddf3e2ae51a67eac9df33f62ca6207b0cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:15:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/30] workflows: the setup job checks app_version; tests for
 it

Upstream's app_version (2026-10-18) is a dispatch input, outside the
encrypted config the runner validates, and "Set custom app version"
pastes it into a sed command (GNU sed's e flag runs commands). Every job
with that step needs the setup job, which already checks version, proto
and build_uuid.

- The setup job's decode step also refuses an app_version that is not
  empty, x.y.z or x.y.z.w (the server's rule), so no build job runs with
  anything else, even when the dispatch did not come from rdgen.
- Tests: the runner check (bad values stop the setup job, the same values
  fail the server rule; this test fails without the check), and the
  dispatch input goes out only when set and bad values get 400.
- ghstub accepts the dispatch inputs the tree's workflows really declare
  (like GitHub) instead of a fixed list, so rdgen sending an input a
  workflow lacks fails the tests.
